Z||000004||88 Database Nut||03-19-2001||02:35 PM||||Thanks Hoop, and Travis for the nice comments.  Travis' Orange Beast is very impressive.  Don's car (not shown) is painted a dark green, and we were sorry we didn't have a white car to complete the colors of the Irish Flag.  It was a lot of fun, and great weather too (sunny, around 65 deg).  It was rainy and cool the last two years.  The nice weather also resulted in a huge crowd.  The parade route this year was through the heart of Buckhead (that's one of the hot singles areas, with quite a few bars).  Lots of "happy" parade watchers as well as kids.<BR>||||reg||1
